WEBVTT

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:07.770
<i>The Teiai Group.</i>

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.680
<i>They rule the Japanese financial 
world from the shadows,</i>

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.520
<i>resolving issues behind the scenes.</i>

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.040
<i>Their true business: black market finance.</i>

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.750
<i>The negligent debtors that 
appear throughout society...</i>

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.570
<i>That is to say, trash. 
A pack of whipped, loser dogs.</i>

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.600
<i>The Teiai Underground Facility.</i>

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.660
<i>Deep underneath Japan, in a location 
its inhabitants have no idea of.</i>

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.380
<i>A forced labor camp, 
where the fallen struggle.</i>

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.420
<i>A truly oppressive environment...</i>

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.640
<i>Indeed, it is truly the underworld!</i>

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.000
<i>The hell that lurks beneath the surface!</i>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.740
<i>This is where they are forced 
to work to repay their debts...</i>

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.110
<i>via heavy labor.</i>

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.530
<i>And Kaiji himself falls here, 
into the underworld.</i>

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.170
<i>And the only thing linking this 
hellscape to the surface is...</i>

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.410
<b>Worker Incentives
One-Day Outside Pass — 500 grand
One-Day Suite Pass (A/C, Bathtub, Videos) — 150 grand</b>

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.290
<i>the one-day outside pass.</i>

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.790
Terrible, Kaiji-kun.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.210
You've got it all wrong. You need 
to learn how to indulge a little.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.720
<b>Labor Log</b>

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.770
<i>Kaiji would end up locked 
in battle against this man.</i>

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.540
<i>And it would give rise to a new legend!</i>

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.140
<i>We turn the clock back to 
before Kaiji arrived...</i>

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.900
<b>One-Day Outside Pass — 500 grand
One-Day Suite Pass (A/C, Bathtub, Videos) — 150 grand
Full Course Dinner — 100 grand
</b>(Western, Japanese, Chinese)
<b>Lunch Combo — 30 grand
20 grand
10 grand</b>

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.770
Man, that one-day pass sounds great...

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:37.440
<i>Perica: the special currency used 
in the underground facility.</i>

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.890
<i>The monthly wages earned by the 
workers here are largely redirected</i>

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.100
<i>to repaying their debts at Teiai.</i>

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.950
<i>After deductions for room and board,</i>

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.310
<i>they are left with only 
91,000 Perica a month.</i>

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:53.050
<i>Meaning that 500,000 Perica 
is a massive amount of money!</i>

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.300
<i>What is it?</i>

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.430
I'll take a one-day outside pass.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.530
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:07.140
A-Again?! How many times does this make?

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.220
That being the case, 
I'll be out all day tomorrow.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:16.250
You guys keep things under control 
down here, Numakawa, Isawa.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.670
Got it.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.950
Have a good day out.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.000
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.700
<i>The man bathed in this sea 
of gazes is the man who,</i>

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.410
<i>while trapped underground,</i>

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.820
<i>earns large amounts of money 
by playing chinchiro,</i>

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.460
<i>obtaining the one-day outside pass... 
The leader of Team E!</i>

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.940
<i>The foreman, Ootsuki!</i>

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.470
<i>The afternoon of the next day,</i>

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.220
<i>on a bench in Hibiya Park...</i>

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.700
<i>Those who receive the one-day pass,</i>

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.470
<i>in order to ensure the secrecy 
of the Teiai underground,</i>

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<i>are put to sleep before being escorted out.</i>

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:58.570
<i>They are then left somewhere, 
in a location of their own request,</i>

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.700
<i>and are observed by men in
black during their excursion.</i>

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.200
<i>When the watch placed on their wrist 
before their leave goes off,</i>

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.470
<i>it marks the start of a 24-hour countdown.</i>

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.210
Time to start...

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.950
Down we go.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.210
<i>Foreman Ootsuki...</i>

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:24.720
<i>The man who rose to the position of Team E's 
foreman in Teiai's Underground Facility.</i>

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.730
<i>This is the tale of the one-day 
outside pass he hoped to obtain</i>

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.430
<i>and his efforts to use his 
limited time effectively.</i>

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:36.940
<i>As we live our modern lives 
constantly pressed for time,</i>

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.680
<i>we can examine our own days by witnessing</i>

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.490
<i>a single day of his, as he attempts 
to live it to its fullest.</i>

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:56.000
<b>1 Day Outside Pass</b>

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:56.000
<b><i>Foreman</i></b>

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.250
<i>Agenda 14
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\hExcursion

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.530
He seems really relaxed.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:28.220
Normally when that alarm goes off, 
they tend to start rushing.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:33.470
Most of them run off, not wanting 
to waste a single second.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.480
They go for pachinko, cabaret clubs, 
steaks, booze, women...

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.970
And when their time does eventually 
run out, they start crying like babies.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.860
But him? He never panics.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.030
Look at him. He's picking fluff off his sweater.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.240
<i>Fluff...</i>

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.830
He really is different. You can tell 
he's gotten used to these excursions.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:00.200
<i>Afterward, he moves on to 
picking fuzz from his socks.</i>

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.730
<i>Fluff, fluff...</i>

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.000
<i>And after a few hours...</i>

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.040
<i>Fluff...</i>

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:10.160
<i>Ootsuki then moves on to a simple dinner,</i>

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.010
<i>then goes to bed...</i>

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:15.270
<b>Apapa Hotel</b>

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.600
<i>at a cut-rate business hotel.</i>

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.610
<i>In no time at all, half of 
his day has been used up.</i>

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.280
<i>The following morning, 
Foreman Ootsuki makes his move.</i>

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.080
All right...

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.210
A suit?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.620
Wait, what? Why would he bother?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.330
He's just going to be put 
underground again! What's the point?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.120
What is he even after?

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.590
I get it! A dress code!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.900
There are lots of high-class places

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:54.560
in Shinbashi and Ginza where you have 
to be dressed properly to even get in.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.810
He's pinning all his desires for 
his one-day pass on one of those!

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.060
He's betting it all on his lunchtime meal!

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.050
A gamble?

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.320
This should be good.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:09.820
What kind of ritzy place will he walk into?

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.330
Oh, there it is.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.830
Standing Bar Soba
<b>Benkei</b>

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.610
A s-soba restaurant with a standing bar?!

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.670
Is there something special about it?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.470
It's got a score of 3.2 on FoodLog...

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:33.470
A totally normal place that specializes 
in serving office workers!

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.050
Welcome!

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.000
Hey, chef, is my mountain 
vegetable soba ready yet?

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:39.980
I'm waiting for my mori!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.760
Coming right up! 
Here's your mountain veggie soba!

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:43.720
What about you, mister?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.060
Z-Zaru...

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.140
Same here.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.750
Two zaru sobas!

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.450
<i>A soba bar at the lunch hour...
A figurative war zone.</i>

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.500
Chef, is my ponzu ready yet?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.420
Got it! One sec!

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:59.310
<i>A battle to obtain a single bowl of soba.</i>

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.280
Let's see...

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.230
He's sitting at the table at a soba bar?

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.890
What the hell's he thinking?

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.530
Excuse me!

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.640
Hey there! What can I get you?

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:13.820
Let's see... I'll get the croquettes, 
the stir-fried vegetables, and...

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.510
<i>He orders individually! Individual items!</i>

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.500
Y'know, let me get the fried shrimp, too.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.520
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:24.190
And this spinach... Can I get it with 
a soft-boiled egg served in a bowl?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.830
<i>And individually...</i>

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:27.310
S-Sure.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.530
And also...

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:29.530
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.540
A draught beer.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:34.520
That'll do.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.780
<i>Draught...</i>

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.430
Uh, sir, did you want any soba?

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:42.640
Oh, I'll get that on the way out.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.040
<i>Psst...</i>

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.540
Here you go.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.430
Your draught beer!

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:51.090
Now, then...

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:03.520
Oh, that hits the spot!

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:05.990
It's the middle of the afternoon...

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.950
I'll have a beer, too.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.580
Idiot! We're not done with our rounds yet!

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.770
B-But...

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:15.650
Can I get a refill?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.700
Another beer. Make it a big mug this time.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.410
<i>Draught...</i>

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:28.290
I see! How diabolical!

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:31.110
He's lording it over them!

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.000
He's relishing in his advantage over 
the office workers who want to,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.550
but can't drink early in the day!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.860
The trick is that suit.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.810
If he was dressed normally and doing this,

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:47.680
they'd think he's just some bum who's 
drinking his ass off because he has no job.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.440
Why would he seem like anything else?

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.070
But look at that...

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:55.720
The second he put that suit on, 
Ootsuki looked like a manager!

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.850
The kind of person with the authority 
to drink in the afternoon!

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.060
Another beer here, please!

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.460
<i>Ootsuki continues to drain the tap!</i>

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:16.310
That seat he's in right now

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:19.720
isn't just a table at a restaurant with 
a bar for standing and eating soba.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:25.320
<i>He reigns over them, as the only person 
in this restaurant allowed to drink.</i>

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:27.980
<i>He sits upon the throne!</i>

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:41.450
It's time, Ootsuki. Get in.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.270
Sure thing. Good work today.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:46.070
<i>The underground prison...</i>

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:47.900
<i>Despite being in a hellish underworld,</i>

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:50.960
<i>he seeks to enjoy his one-day 
excursions to their utmost.</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.030
<i>From the bottom, he seeks the top!</i>

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:58.970
<i>But where will Foreman Ootsuki's 
next one-day pass take him?</i>

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:03.850
Can I get a refill?

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:10.110
<i>The head of Team E, Foreman Ootsuki,</i>

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.980
<i>has been set free with another 
one-day outside pass!</i>

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.490
<i>This is Kinshi-cho...</i>

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:36.500
<i>Bask, bask, bask, bask...</i>

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:31.750
<i>Ootsuki is then struck by an unexpected 
desire to bask in the sun.</i>

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.530
<i>And sleeps again, like a rock, 
for eight hours!</i>

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:41.060
<i>Once the sun sets and his 
surroundings grow dark,</i>

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:44.260
<i>he finally rises. Ultimately on this day,</i>

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.010
<i>he eats a simple dinner</i>

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.020
<i>and rests for the night at 
inexpensive business hotel.</i>

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.900
<i>Once it's nearly noon, he's on the move.</i>

00:11:55.900 --> 00:12:00.410
<i>I think I've got time for one more 
meal before I hit my time limit...</i>

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:03.290
<i>So I need to eat something 
I know I'll enjoy.</i>

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:08.210
<i>Since I'm in Kinshi-cho, 
I'd better head to Jajaen and—</i>

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:12.070
The more and harder you struggle,

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:15.170
the more and harder you get stuck!

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:19.800
But don't you give up!

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.780
<i>This town hasn't changed at all.</i>

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:22.920
<i>Kinshi-cho...</i>

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:27.930
<i>This is actually the town that Ootsuki 
worked in to support himself as a student.</i>

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.680
I know!

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:32.930
The crab fried rice at Daikoku-ya!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.430
That's it, that's the ticket!

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.690
I remember it now!

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:40.320
<b>Chinese Cuisine
Daikoku-ya</b>

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.320
<i>The Chinese restaurant Daikoku-ya.</i>

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:43.320
<i>The chef is famous for his stern attitude,</i>

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.230
<i>but when students order the crab fried rice,</i>

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:50.600
<i>he provides them with an extra large 
serving at no extra cost, 1.5x the usual!</i>

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.970
<i>A smooth move on his part!</i>

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:55.550
<i>This crab fried rice was an incredible feast</i>

00:12:55.550 --> 00:13:00.960
<i>for Ootsuki, whose daily poverty had him 
living on chocolate chip cookie sticks.</i>

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.090
<i>A delicious feast that 
would appear before him!</i>

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.970
<i>A cherished dish from his memories!</i>

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:12.970
<b>Chinese Cuisine
Daikoku-ya</b>

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:12.340
<i>It's still here. And it hasn't changed 
at all from back in the day.</i>

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:15.690
Hey, welcome.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.240
<i>That's right, he'd always say that.</i>

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.840
Quit screwing around! 
There's no way that's true!

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:23.740
I'm telling you, it's true!

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:30.610
It was mahjong, but the 
pieces were transparent...

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:29.490
<i>And this place still serves a 
bunch of obnoxious students, too.</i>

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:39.890
<i>His hair's gone white, but the 
chef hasn't changed, either.</i>

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:45.470
<i>And these menus with the wrinkled corners!</i>

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.120
<i>He's still using them?</i>

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.100
<i>The menu itself hasn't changed, either!</i>

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:52.130
<i>And of course...</i>

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.100
<i>There it is!</i>

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.850
<b>Ankake Yakisoba
Shrimp Fried Rice
</b>Omelette Rice
<b>Crab Fried Rice
Gyoza (Grilled)
Gyoza (Soup)</b>

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.850
<i>The crab fried rice from my memor—</i>

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:57.990
<i>Psst...</i>

00:13:57.990 --> 00:13:58.850
What is this?

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:05.360
Omelette Rice

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:03.100
<i>Between the shrimp and crab fried rice...</i>

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.360
<i>Omelette rice?</i>

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.360
<i>That wasn't there before.</i>

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.610
<i>And more like...</i>

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.930
<i>Wouldn't that just be regular omelette rice?</i>

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:14.920
<i>No, no, no, no!</i>

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:18.100
<i>Even if it is, why would they be 
serving it at a Chinese restaurant?</i>

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.120
<b>Psst...</b>

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:21.480
What can I get you?

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.170
Uh, well...

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.420
<i>When using the one-day pass,</i>

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:31.300
<i>the most dangerous thing is to 
choose your actions poorly.</i>

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:34.980
<i>If curiosity gets the better of you and 
you order something that tastes bad,</i>

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.680
<i>it will sink its claws into you.</i>

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:43.060
<i>I guess he probably added it later 
and just wrote it into the menu...</i>

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:49.150
<i>But man, I'm really curious 
about how it's squeezed in here...</i>

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:49.820
Omelette Rice

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.450
<i>Wait, no!</i>

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:56.370
<i>An adventure out here will 
cost me days underground!</i>

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.090
<i>I need to stick to the plan.</i>

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.910
Well, let's see...

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.290
Omelette Rice

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:05.440
Can I get this omelette rice?

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.170
<i>Psst, Psst...</i>

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:13.430
<i>Why the hell didn't I ask for the crab 
fried rice?! Why the omelette rice?!</i>

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:19.430
<i>Was it too strong?! By just enough?</i>

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.530
<i>My curiosity overwhelmed 
my desire for safety?!</i>

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.210
And that'll be it?

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:29.800
Uh, well...

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:31.820
Yeah.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.670
<i>Psst, psst, psst...</i>

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.380
It'll be just a bit.

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:41.270
<i>Wait, what was that?</i>

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.830
<b>Psst...</b>

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:46.120
<i>Did I make the wrong move after all?!</i>

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.570
<i>Should I have just stuck 
with the crab fried rice?!</i>

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:50.020
<i>Psst...</i>

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:51.590
Here's your hot towel.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.800
No, I can't let it bother me!

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:07.650
<i>The most important thing about these 
one-day excursions is keeping your cool.</i>

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.830
<i>Stay calm, stay calm...</i>

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:18.910
<i>No matter the circumstances, 
as long as you stay calm,</i>

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.380
<i>you can reach safety in one piece.</i>

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:25.830
<i>It might seem as though Ootsuki 
has randomly made this order,</i>

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:32.170
<b>Ankake Yakisoba
Shrimp Fried Rice
</b>Omelette Rice
<b>Crab Fried Rice
Gyoza (Grilled)
Gyoza (Soup)</b>

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:32.170
<i>but it was not entirely a reckless 
gamble. The reason being...</i>

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:37.160
<i>The most popular items on the 
menu here at Daikoku-ya are</i>

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:44.690
<b>Chinese Cuisine
Daikoku-ya</b>

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.370
<i>#4: Lettuce fried rice.</i>

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.310
<b>#4: Lettuce fried rice</b>

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.930
<b>#3: Mixed fried rice</b>

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:41.240
<i>#3: Mixed fried rice.</i>

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.770
<b>#2: Shrimp fried rice</b>

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:43.030
<i>#2: Shrimp fried rice.</i>

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:45.210
<i>And #1...</i>

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.520
<i>Crab fried rice!</i>

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.130
<i>In other words, all fried dishes.</i>

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:52.940
<i>If you're curious, #5 is crispy yakisoba.</i>

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.620
<i>In other words, fried dishes are 
rock-solid here at Daikoku-ya!</i>

00:16:58.100 --> 00:16:59.910
<i>You can't go wrong!</i>

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:02.910
<i>Yeah! When I think of it that way,</i>

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.350
<i>omelette rice is fried, too...</i>

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.070
<i>There's no way it can be bad.</i>

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:13.100
<i>My curiosity might've 
gotten the better of me,</i>

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:16.430
<i>but I'll be generous and allow that this time!</i>

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:20.510
<i>And so, the moment arrives: lunchtime!</i>

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.170
<i>The location: Daikoku-ya in Kinshi-cho!</i>

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.030
Here you go.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.190
<i>It's time...</i>

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.070
Your omelette rice.

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:29.940
<i>Right, omelette ri—</i>

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:36.190
<i>It's not just omelette rice?!</i>

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:40.020
<i>It's an omelette </i>and<i> rice?! 
That's what "omelette rice" is?!</i>

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:43.130
<i>He's struck with sorrow! 
An unexpected comprehension error!</i>

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:50.020
<i>Ootsuki spends 50 seconds in a daze.</i>

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.000
<i>However!</i>

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:54.010
<i>The time limit creeps ever closer!</i>

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:57.990
<i>He's on the verge of giving up in 
what seems like a wasted lunchtime!</i>

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.510
<i>What a pitiful dish...</i>

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:04.760
<i>Like something you could 
get at a school cafeteria.</i>

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:10.390
<i>The sensation sends a 
buzz through his system.</i>

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.420
<i>What's with this omelette?</i>

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.780
<i>The inside isn't cooked all the 
way through, so it's fluffy.</i>

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.450
<i>And now that I look closely, look at that!</i>

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:23.280
<i>It's stuffed with stewed pork and onions!</i>

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:26.890
<i>You'd never see that kind of thing 
in a Western-style omelette!</i>

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.220
<i>I-It's good!</i>

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:35.090
<i>And there's some of that mixed in, too!</i>

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:44.350
<b>Wei Ba</b>

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.410
<i>Wei Ba!</i>

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:39.000
<i>Wei Ba!</i>

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:42.170
<i>The Chinese soup stock said 
to be the ultimate seasoning!</i>

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:43.640
<i>The soft-kneaded type!</i>

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:49.350
<i>I was worried about the lack of ketchup, 
but this should more than suffice!</i>

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:56.660
<i>It makes the rice go down so smoothly!</i>

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:57.210
So good!

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.030
<i>And before he knows it, Ootsuki...</i>

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:04.740
<i>has cleaned his dishes of omelette 
and rice in only a few minutes!</i>

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.540
<i>That was fantastic, to my surprise.</i>

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:14.680
<i>I was a bit worried there, but that 
was satisfying in its own way.</i>

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:16.550
<i>Although...</i>

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:22.800
<i>It's a shame I'll be going back 
without having any crab fried rice.</i>

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:23.550
Here you go.

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:26.680
A mini crab fried rice.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.720
Oh, no, I didn't order this.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:32.710
Wait, really?

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:35.960
You used to always order this,

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.130
so I made it by accident.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.950
Well, it's on the house, then!

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.070
Wait... Chef?

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:50.460
<i>It's been 25 years... 
and he still remembers me?</i>

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.070
<i>An overwhelming sense of nostalgia.</i>

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.890
<i>Memories of his youth stir.</i>

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.240
<i>He's sent on a time trip...</i>

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:13.910
<i>Things that haven't changed 
with the passing of time:</i>

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:16.980
<i>human kindness, Kinshi-cho...</i>

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.480
<i>and crab fried rice!</i>

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.990
<i>I never would have imagined...</i>

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.810
<i>He receives his first student 
discount in 25 years!</i>

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:34.500
<i>In the end, he leaves the 
restaurant in high spirits.</i>

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:45.510
<i>He borrows a man in black's smartphone 
to find a restaurant rating site.</i>

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:48.260
<i>For Daikoku-ya in Kinshi-cho, he gives...</i>

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.850
<i>Five stars for value, five stars for food.</i>

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:53.180
<b>Kinshi-cho                  Daikoku-ya</b>

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:53.180
<b>Value:

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.180
<i>For the restaurant's atmosphere...</i>

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:56.960
<i>Three stars.</i>

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:02.440
<b>There were a lot of students eating there,
and it was rather loud.</b>

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.630
<i>Even when in the clutches 
of the underground prison,</i>

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:09.540
<i>he seeks to maximize the enjoyment 
of his one-day excursions.</i>

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.900
<i>From the bottom, he seeks the top!</i>

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:18.260
<i>Where will Foreman Ootsuki's 
next one-day pass take him?</i>

00:22:55.750 --> 00:22:57.860
<i>Next time, "Playing Hard."</i>

00:22:56.620 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Playing Hard</b>
